{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfCAYmyc92a8U6c7inFw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011Yahjau9G8SUP9wPfy5zVW","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub","prompt":"List every file in this directory and describe what each file is for. Explain how a game integrates with the hub: the protocol, required functions, the exit-interview / run record / catalogue fields it expects, and any README instructions. Quote key API names and file names."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7250,"cache_read_input_tokens":17754,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7250,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15bc258b-d291-4236-a54a-0598527cb274","uuid":"f9d338c8-155f-4b56-9df9-6943dd0f8634","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:18:55.332Z","request_id":"req_011CgfCAY1b2ESJ1DKTZvNHu","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011Yahjau9G8SUP9wPfy5zVW":{"url":"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub","prompt":"List every file in this directory and describe what each file is for. Explain how a game integrates with the hub: the protocol, required functions, the exit-interview / run record / catalogue fields it expects, and any README instructions. Quote key API names and file names."}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011Yahjau9G8SUP9wPfy5zVW","type":"tool_result","content":"## Files in this directory\n\nThe page lists these entries, but it doesn't describe the contents of most of them:\n\n- **`examples/`**: A folder. The page doesn't say what it contains.\n- **`README.md`**: The protocol specification, \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1,\" which covers modes, rounds, tags, the client API, messaging, rules, and testing.\n- **`bridge.js`**: Fetched alongside the harness for testing. The page doesn't describe its role in detail.\n- **`harness.html`**: A test harness that plays the hub. It loads a game 1–4 times on a simulated network and runs the same checks the hub runs when a game joins the library.\n- **`retrofit.md`**: Listed only by name. The page doesn't describe it.\n- **`round.js`**: Fetched alongside the harness for testing. The page doesn't describe its role in detail.\n- **`session.js`**: The client. A game includes it unmodified as the first script in `<head>`, after `<meta charset>`.\n\nThe page says \"View all files,\" so this directory may contain more files than the ones shown.\n\n## How a game integrates\n\n**Tags** in the game's `<head>`:\n- `hub:session` (set to `1`)\n- `hub:session-players` (format `MIN-MAX`)\n- `hub:session-mode` (`parallel`, `ghost`, or `shared-world`)\n- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`\n\nOptional tags are `hub:session-minutes` and `hub:webgpu`.\n\n**Client calls:**\n- `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats })` returns a promise of `info`, or `null` if there is no hub.\n- `AIHub.ready()` is called once, when the round can start.\n- `AIHub.time()` gives the shared timeline.\n- `AIHub.on(event, fn)` handles `start`, `message`, `leave`, `time-up`, and `end`.\n- `AIHub.progress()` reports standing in parallel and ghost modes.\n- `AIHub.result()` reports the final result in parallel and ghost modes, once.\n- `AIHub.finish()` reports standings in shared-world mode, from the host only, once.\n- `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` sends messages between copies in ghost and shared-world modes.\n- `AIHub.rng(label)` gives numbers that match on every copy.\n- `AIHub.fail(message)` is called when the game can't run in the browser.\n\n**Rules** include no direct network traffic outside the hub, no communication between players, no `alert`/`confirm`/`prompt`, and no navigating away.\n\n**Testing:** Serve `harness.html` next to the game and open it with the game's name and player count. The game passes when `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true.\n\n## Fields not covered\n\nThe page doesn't mention exit-interview, run-record, or catalogue fields. The closest equivalents are the `info` object returned by `connect()`, the `end` reason values, and the optional `stats` and `awards` fields on `result()` and `finish()`."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15bc258b-d291-4236-a54a-0598527cb274","uuid":"8c301405-4d90-4923-9029-0fb86af03ac6","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:19:03.513Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":287988,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"## Files in this directory\n\nThe page lists these entries, but it doesn't describe the contents of most of them:\n\n- **`examples/`**: A folder. The page doesn't say what it contains.\n- **`README.md`**: The protocol specification, \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1,\" which covers modes, rounds, tags, the client API, messaging, rules, and testing.\n- **`bridge.js`**: Fetched alongside the harness for testing. The page doesn't describe its role in detail.\n- **`harness.html`**: A test harness that plays the hub. It loads a game 1–4 times on a simulated network and runs the same checks the hub runs when a game joins the library.\n- **`retrofit.md`**: Listed only by name. The page doesn't describe it.\n- **`round.js`**: Fetched alongside the harness for testing. The page doesn't describe its role in detail.\n- **`session.js`**: The client. A game includes it unmodified as the first script in `<head>`, after `<meta charset>`.\n\nThe page says \"View all files,\" so this directory may contain more files than the ones shown.\n\n## How a game integrates\n\n**Tags** in the game's `<head>`:\n- `hub:session` (set to `1`)\n- `hub:session-players` (format `MIN-MAX`)\n- `hub:session-mode` (`parallel`, `ghost`, or `shared-world`)\n- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`\n\nOptional tags are `hub:session-minutes` and `hub:webgpu`.\n\n**Client calls:**\n- `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats })` returns a promise of `info`, or `null` if there is no hub.\n- `AIHub.ready()` is called once, when the round can start.\n- `AIHub.time()` gives the shared timeline.\n- `AIHub.on(event, fn)` handles `start`, `message`, `leave`, `time-up`, and `end`.\n- `AIHub.progress()` reports standing in parallel and ghost modes.\n- `AIHub.result()` reports the final result in parallel and ghost modes, once.\n- `AIHub.finish()` reports standings in shared-world mode, from the host only, once.\n- `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` sends messages between copies in ghost and shared-world modes.\n- `AIHub.rng(label)` gives numbers that match on every copy.\n- `AIHub.fail(message)` is called when the game can't run in the browser.\n\n**Rules** include no direct network traffic outside the hub, no communication between players, no `alert`/`confirm`/`prompt`, and no navigating away.\n\n**Testing:** Serve `harness.html` next to the game and open it with the game's name and player count. The game passes when `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true.\n\n## Fields not covered\n\nThe page doesn't mention exit-interview, run-record, or catalogue fields. The closest equivalents are the `info` object returned by `connect()`, the `end` reason values, and the optional `stats` and `awards` fields on `result()` and `finish()`.","durationMs":8178,"url":"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011Yahjau9G8SUP9wPfy5zVW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BwAeZjH3KnuXm8p3xCXUn5","type":"tool_result","content":"## Files in `dist/handoff/`\n\nThe page lists these entries. Its \"View all files\" link suggests there may be more.\n\n| Entry | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `README.md` | Start-here guide for the engine handoff. |\n| `API.md` | The API card: a complete starter game, coordinate meanings per view, rules, common mistakes, and the API by area. |\n| `API-INDEX.md` | Index of every public engine name with signature, units, and defaults. Meant to be searched, not read whole. |\n| `AI_GUIDE.md` | Recipes by genre, target look, frame order, heights, and recorded sessions. |\n| `my-3d2dge.js` | The full engine in one readable file, with no dependencies. |\n| `my-3d2dge-agent.js` | The lighter \"agent edition\" of the engine, with a shorter manual in its header. |\n| `modules/` | Optional engine modules, each loaded after the agent edition. |\n| `index.html` | Page entry point (not described in detail on the page). |\n| `package.json` | Pins Playwright for the tools. |\n| `game/` | Template game: `index.html` (plays it), `game.js` (its code), `test.mjs` (headless test). |\n| `kits/` | 2D genre starter games. Each `<id>.js` is a game, `<id>.html` plays it, and `test.mjs` runs it headless. `README.md` is the table of kits. |\n| `docs/ASSETS.md` | Asset card for still objects and materials. Read before drawing objects. |\n| `src/assets/` | Asset store of CC0-derived sets and catalogs (Kenney, KayKit, ambientCG). |\n| `tools/check.mjs` | Plays a game in headless Chromium, switches views, and reports errors and snapshots. |\n| `tools/filmstrip.mjs` | Records frames into one image to judge motion. |\n| `tools/replay.mjs` | Replays a recorded play session exactly. |\n| `tools/asset-find.mjs` | Searches the core library and the store. |\n| `tools/asset-sheet.mjs` | Draws an object in every view and lints it. |\n| `tools/asset-set.mjs` | Cuts a few entries into a set of their own (uses `asset-lib.mjs`). |\n\n## Entry points and usage\n\n- Open `game/index.html` in a browser, or serve the folder (for example, `npx serve`).\n- Run `node game/test.mjs` for a headless test with no browser.\n- Run `node kits/test.mjs arcade` to run a kit headlessly.\n- Run `node tools/check.mjs game/index.html` to play in a browser and get errors, screenshots, and a snapshot.\n\n## Key API names\n\n- `E.Game`, with `new E.Game({ menu: { items, settings, controls, quit } })` for menu customization\n- `game.start({ boot: { steps } })` for heavy setup\n- `game.advance(seconds)`, which runs fixed 1/120 s steps\n- `game.input.tap('jump')` and `game.input.hold('right', false)`\n- `game.debug = { snapshot() {...}, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }`\n- `game.stop()`, `game.start()`, `game.dispose()`\n- `r.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing })`\n- `map.solid`, `E.MATERIALS`\n- `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-furniture'])`\n- `E.session`, for replaying recorded sessions\n\n## Bundling into a single HTML file\n\nThe page gives only one instruction: to hand a single file to someone, \"inline the two scripts into the page.\" It names no build tool, so the exact steps are not in this content.\n\n## Note on scope\n\nThe 3D engine (three.js and Rapier) and its kits are not in this folder. The page points to the site and repository for them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15bc258b-d291-4236-a54a-0598527cb274","uuid":"38300c01-e9d6-4ba7-8172-c03fb111e4b6","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:19:04.728Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":234277,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"## Files in `dist/handoff/`\n\nThe page lists these entries. Its \"View all files\" link suggests there may be more.\n\n| Entry | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `README.md` | Start-here guide for the engine handoff. |\n| `API.md` | The API card: a complete starter game, coordinate meanings per view, rules, common mistakes, and the API by area. |\n| `API-INDEX.md` | Index of every public engine name with signature, units, and defaults. Meant to be searched, not read whole. |\n| `AI_GUIDE.md` | Recipes by genre, target look, frame order, heights, and recorded sessions. |\n| `my-3d2dge.js` | The full engine in one readable file, with no dependencies. |\n| `my-3d2dge-agent.js` | The lighter \"agent edition\" of the engine, with a shorter manual in its header. |\n| `modules/` | Optional engine modules, each loaded after the agent edition. |\n| `index.html` | Page entry point (not described in detail on the page). |\n| `package.json` | Pins Playwright for the tools. |\n| `game/` | Template game: `index.html` (plays it), `game.js` (its code), `test.mjs` (headless test). |\n| `kits/` | 2D genre starter games. Each `<id>.js` is a game, `<id>.html` plays it, and `test.mjs` runs it headless. `README.md` is the table of kits. |\n| `docs/ASSETS.md` | Asset card for still objects and materials. Read before drawing objects. |\n| `src/assets/` | Asset store of CC0-derived sets and catalogs (Kenney, KayKit, ambientCG). |\n| `tools/check.mjs` | Plays a game in headless Chromium, switches views, and reports errors and snapshots. |\n| `tools/filmstrip.mjs` | Records frames into one image to judge motion. |\n| `tools/replay.mjs` | Replays a recorded play session exactly. |\n| `tools/asset-find.mjs` | Searches the core library and the store. |\n| `tools/asset-sheet.mjs` | Draws an object in every view and lints it. |\n| `tools/asset-set.mjs` | Cuts a few entries into a set of their own (uses `asset-lib.mjs`). |\n\n## Entry points and usage\n\n- Open `game/index.html` in a browser, or serve the folder (for example, `npx serve`).\n- Run `node game/test.mjs` for a headless test with no browser.\n- Run `node kits/test.mjs arcade` to run a kit headlessly.\n- Run `node tools/check.mjs game/index.html` to play in a browser and get errors, screenshots, and a snapshot.\n\n## Key API names\n\n- `E.Game`, with `new E.Game({ menu: { items, settings, controls, quit } })` for menu customization\n- `game.start({ boot: { steps } })` for heavy setup\n- `game.advance(seconds)`, which runs fixed 1/120 s steps\n- `game.input.tap('jump')` and `game.input.hold('right', false)`\n- `game.debug = { snapshot() {...}, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }`\n- `game.stop()`, `game.start()`, `game.dispose()`\n- `r.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing })`\n- `map.solid`, `E.MATERIALS`\n- `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-furniture'])`\n- `E.session`, for replaying recorded sessions\n\n## Bundling into a single HTML file\n\nThe page gives only one instruction: to hand a single file to someone, \"inline the two scripts into the page.\" It names no build tool, so the exact steps are not in this content.\n\n## Note on scope\n\nThe 3D engine (three.js and Rapier) and its kits are not in this folder. The page points to the site and repository for them.","durationMs":9911,"url":"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/tree/main/dist/handoff"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BwAeZjH3KnuXm8p3xCXUn5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
