{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013c4TRNLKne4KnKMGw5ptS6","type":"tool_result","content":"397:- `game.particles.text(x, y, z, text, color = '#fff2c4', o = {})`: floating number or word: text(x, y, z, '12', color, { scale: 2, bounce: true }) (bounce: lands and holds, Final Fantasy style)\n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and applied; it shows on the settings screen. Returns its value\n745:- `map.center(cx, cy)`: the world point at a cell's center\n820:- `flow.dir(x, y, fx, fy)`: normalized ground direction to walk from (x, y) toward the target (straight at it where the field doesn't reach)\n821:- `flow.next(x, y)` †: the next cell to head for from (x, y): { x, y, z (its center and top), kind: 'walk' | 'climb' | 'drop' | 'jump', edge (how far (x, y) is from the side of its cell it leaves by) }, or null where the field doesn't reach (or at the target). An AI standing on the ground presses jump for a 'climb' or a 'jump' once edge is under its radius plus a little (E.Mover climbs or leaps; a press in the air would be kept for the landing)\n822:- `flow.update(x, y)`: aim the field at a world point; it rebuilds only when the target's cell or the map (map.version) changes\n823:- `flow.climb`: how much higher a next-door top may be (an agent that climbs walls)\n824:- `flow.d`: each cell's distance in steps to the target cell (1e9 where it can't get there), row by row\n825:- `flow.drop`: how much lower (an agent that hops down)\n826:- `flow.jump` †: the widest gap jumped (world units, 0 = none)\n827:- `flow.jumpDrop`, `flow.jumpRise` †: how much higher and lower a jump may land\n828:- `flow.map`: the map it paths over\n829:- `flow.step`: the height difference walked over freely (2)\n830:- `flow.tx = -1`, `flow.ty = -1`: the target's cell\n831:- `flow.version = -1`: the map's version it was built for\n1058:- `game.audio.mute(on = !this.muted)`: toggle (or set) mute; returns the new state\n1073:- `game.audio.muted = false`: true while mute() is on\n1135:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n1138:- `menu.update()`: move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled\n1186:- `shell.toast(title, text = '', seconds = 4)` †: a message that slides in at the top for a few seconds\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-191849__xe8b2f0/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15bc258b-d291-4236-a54a-0598527cb274","uuid":"4506a8e1-47cc-40e4-b873-f396ac31eb70","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:23:57.887Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"397:- `game.particles.text(x, y, z, text, color = '#fff2c4', o = {})`: floating number or word: text(x, y, z, '12', color, { scale: 2, bounce: true }) (bounce: lands and holds, Final Fantasy style)\n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and applied; it shows on the settings screen. Returns its value\n745:- `map.center(cx, cy)`: the world point at a cell's center\n820:- `flow.dir(x, y, fx, fy)`: normalized ground direction to walk from (x, y) toward the target (straight at it where the field doesn't reach)\n821:- `flow.n